Based on the screenshot and the description, Chrome’s autofill is applying its native “sky-blue” background to our `<input>`, which then makes the “clear” (X) icon (rendered in white) inaccessible due to poor contrast. We need to override that autofill style and force the input back to our normal background and text colors.

There are two places we ship a Search component:

1. The React `<Search>` in  
   `packages/react/src/components/Search/Search.js`

2. The “vanilla JS” Search in  
   `packages/components/src/components/search/search.js`

In the React version we can simply inject an inline style on the `<input>` that neutralizes the autofill background. In the vanilla JS version we’ll inject a small `<style>` block into the document head (once) that resets the `:-webkit-autofill` on all our `.bx--search-input`s.

