With these two patches applied:

- The React `<Search>` will render its input with an inline `WebkitBoxShadow` that covers up the autofill coloration and a `WebkitTextFillColor: inherit` so text remains readable.
- The vanilla-JS Search will inject a one-time `<style>` rule into the document’s `<head>` to reset any `.bx--search-input:-webkit-autofill` back to white (or whatever your normal background is) and preserve text color.
